Chromium: enable -Wno-unused-but-set-global and -Wno-deprecated-declarations on BSD.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD.
Apply after other build/config/compiler patches.
NetBSD official builds use clang 23 with -Werror; under NDEBUG many
debug globals are set but their readers are compiled out. Upstream only
adds -Wno-unused-but-set-global when !is_bsd; enable for BSD too.
SDK pkg expat also deprecates many XML_* APIs (SkXMLParser,
SkFontMgr_android_parser), which floods -Wdeprecated-declarations under
-Werror; silence that in the same !is_wasm block.

--- a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -1980,13 +1980,18 @@
       "-Wno-nontrivial-memcall",
     ]
 
-    if (!is_wasm && !is_bsd) {
+    # EmberBSD: NetBSD target uses clang 23 with -Werror; official/NDEBUG
+    # leaves debug globals set-but-unused (icu_util, logging, trace_log, …).
+    # Upstream gates these -Wno-* behind !is_bsd; enable them for BSD too.
+    if (!is_wasm) {
       cflags += [
         # TODO(crbug.com/432275627): Fix and re-enable.
         "-Wno-uninitialized-const-pointer",
 
         # TODO(crbug.com/495753203): Fix and re-enable.
         "-Wno-unused-but-set-global",
+        # EmberBSD: SDK pkg expat newer than Chromium; XML_* APIs deprecated.
+        "-Wno-deprecated-declarations",
       ]
     }
 
